06-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:47:Decisions: The rejection-then-fix cycle with the architect continues to catch real defects (r1's recursion probe found a hole my own probes missed). Collection-call syntax `(v 1)/(m :k)/(k m)` — the gate round's real feature — survives; only its routing was reconciled with the convention.\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:48:Verification: as above; full JVM suite (minus :slow) on v2 in flight; astra r2 dispatched (resume, same thread) with /tmp/h2_reconcile_v2.diff; shiva dao.stream gate at the dgram fix branch: clj 538/0 ✓, cljd 457/0 ✓ (the Linux datagram fix works), cljs lane errored on missing node_modules (scratch-clone infra, npm install + rerun in flight).\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:49:Delegates: architect/astra (r1 deny, r2 pending, thread 01a199e5-6c7e-7263-821d-f78529f35b7c).\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:50:Next: full-suite + astra r2 → on grant: commit the reconciliation, push, shiva Node/Dart lanes at the signed commit → merge order per Workflow 2. dgram: cljs lane green → dao.stream precondition satisfied → merge fix/datagram-linux-exclusive-binder to master (rebase onto moved master first, rerun the gate if the rebase is non-trivial).\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:52:## 2026-11-02 14:05:00 +07 — astra GRANTED (r4); reconciliation committed (6f4a3c17 + ea18c8e4) and pushed; dgram fix LANDED to master\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:57:Done: (1) astra r2 verdict: both code blockers CLOSED, but the range denied for record LOSS in 0bf8bc4e — the rebase seat's \"merge-resolution\" had dropped known-gaps rows (both JVM recursion findings, jolt ping-after-close, the common-call arbitration section, J5c's closed disposition), 11 sections of the python-track log, and rewritten two collab/ paths to a nonexistent archive/ tree. (2) Union repair: known-gaps byte-identical to origin/master; python log = master + the branch's THREE branch-only sections (S3 chain, two-tier policy, per-compiler subsystem split). My r3 extraction under-counted (cut the tail from the already-modified working file — caught by astra r3, corrected by extracting from HEAD:). astra r4: SIGN-OFF GRANTED for 0dc5d7af..0bf8bc4e + the four-file reconciliation; conditions: suite result recorded before commit ✓, final-commit shiva Node/Dart lanes (running at ea18c8e4), the kernel gate's unexercised arities stay blocked ✓. (3) Full JVM suite on the reconciled tree: 4821 tests / 300,901 assertions, exactly 3 failures — ALL in test-kernel-differential-gate's own blocked-state assertions (the honest BLOCKED gate). Recorded drift for hardening-3: live unexercised function/arities=58 vs the evidence's recorded 20 — the gate stays blocked, its arity accounting needs re-derivation under the reconciled compiler. (4) Committed 6f4a3c17 (ledger restoration) + ea18c8e4 (the reconciliation; the pre-commit formatter rewrote both files, re-verified 122/0 at the commit). Pushed yang-hardening2 over the stale pre-rebase remote lineage (diff vs mine: 7400 files/53k deletions missing — the remote predated the rebase). (5) dgram lane: the shiva cljs 2-failure suspicion resolved — master ran the SAME lane green in the same clone (the cross-node corpus test is timing-flaky, and needed npm-installed node_modules in a fresh scratch clone); rebased the fix onto master (3219bc3b), reran the full dao.stream gate: clj 538/0, cljs 528/0, cljd 457/0 — the merge precondition met on all three lanes with the fixed datagram test passing on Linux. MERGED to master a226423d and pushed.\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:58:Decisions: The r3 correction is recorded because it is exactly the failure mode the union rule exists for — I unioned from the wrong tree and the architect caught it. Kernel-gate drift is recorded, not papered over: the gate's blocked status is preserved per the sign-off's condition 3.\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:60:Delegates: architect/astra (r2 deny, r3 deny-partial, r4 grant; thread 01a199e5).\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:71:Delegates: architect/astra (r4 grant, thread 01a199e5).\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:101:Done: (1) The kernel-gate evidence refresh ran on shiva at master (the documented write-kernel-gate-evidence! procedure; the first dispatch died on ssh heredoc quoting before the JVM started — rerun succeeded). Verdict: the gate stays :blocked with 100 passing agreements unchanged; 107 credited executions (39 direct — IDENTICAL to the old evidence — + 68 named integrations, down from 106) and 58 unexercised admitted arities. Drift classification: the reconciliation UN-CREDITED 38 named-integration trace paths; all 20 previously-recorded unexercised arities remain; no agreement moved. (2) Regenerated evidence committed (d5d56ca3) after local + shiva verification: the gate test's accounting assertion now passes; master's suite failures in the gate drop 3 -> 2. The 2 remaining: the by-design blocked assertion, and the recorded-deviation bookkeeping — the refresh WRITER regenerates :recorded-portability-boundaries as [] and drops the two declared departures (elab-after-qed / check-after-qed, boundary :nonportable-host-value, upstream embeds clojure.core/meta in error data) from fixture statuses; the full declared records survive in git history. Deliberately NOT hand-fabricated: declared dispositions belong to the writer fix the architect designs. (3) Hardening-3 design dispatched to astra (new thread, brief collab/1793770000000-architect-hardening-3-design.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md): fixture-closure strategy for the 58 (clustered: proof elaboration is the largest; presyntax; normalization; syntax; typing; env/unparser