ia merge-base; kimi r3 in flight (stream-json + --verbose per the recipe as corrected by the other seat's docs commit).\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:357:Delegates: architect/kimi-k3.1-pro (r3 rulings).\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:358:Next: kimi r3 -> architect rulings into the adoption plan -> coordinate with the TS/PHP orchestrator for the pinned runtime -> bounded engineering briefs -> cross-language cases after all frontends pinned. CONCURRENT ORCHESTRATION maintained: slice-9 gate committed on its branch; hardening-program-2 + CIC Phase 1 remain parked for owner; no file conflicts with the new track (different worktrees, disjoint paths).\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:360:## 2026-10-29 23:57:26 +07 — kimi r3 rulings DELIVERED (A1-A5): descriptors for every source fn, universal routing, empty named vector, entry-boundary outcome conversion, private helpers stay\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:365:Done: kimi r3 (session stream in collab/1793292667828-*; one CLI retry: --verbose is not a kimi flag, contrary to my earlier recipe note) ruled: A1 every admitted Clojure source function publishes an immutable descriptor {:yang.call/entry <new unary record-closure> :clj/type :function} — NOT the body closure, NOT deferred to export time, not a second direct-closure kind; A2 EVERY source application routes through the common projection (no descriptor-check fast path as conformance; fast paths optional optimizations only, conformance exercises the unoptimized path); A3 :yang.call/named [] always supplied (empty vector; nonempty named -> guest binding error before body); A4 the outcome-model <-> raise-exit conversion sits in EVERY generated entry/caller bridge (callee: ok->value, error->raise; caller: condition->outcome propagation; no tuple-as-value leak); A5 dsg__ temps/library privates/kernel context stay non-descriptors (source publication is the distinction). Additional obligations: data-with-the-key is not callable; anonymous/higher-order fns need the same convention; arity checked in the entry before body; macros acquire no entries; native closures admitted only explicitly; unsupported-surface refusals preserved; slice-9 gate unaffected.\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:367:Verification: kimi r3 exit 0, findings extracted (6.3KB) and synced.\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:368:Delegates: architect/kimi-k3.1-pro (r3).\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:376:Done: Owner authorized continuing the hardening (\"ok continue with hardening yang.clojure then\"). The six gate blockers (slice-9's named dependencies) are the program: (1) manifest admission dispositions; (2) missing stdlib admissions (butlast/last/nth/var?/with-meta/string? + whatever the evidence graph repeats); (3) gensym freshness (explicit supply with a counter); (4) free-vars context adaptation fix (upstream's (second def-env) shape); (5) the real unfold-implicit try path; (6) opacity atom -> context field. Round 1 (all six, dependency order) dispatched to codex/gpt-6.1-sol in yang-h2, based on 7dc18478. The gate stays red during this program; it goes green only in its own final verification slice. The common-call track remains parked on the coordinating owner's pinned runtime (independent worktree; no conflicts).\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:404:## 2026-10-30 20:39:45 +07 — adoption S1 glm review: 2 P1 + 2 P2 + 2 P3; contradiction escalated to kimi r4 arbitration\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:409:Done: glm adoption-S1 review (session e1599324, findings synced to main collab/1793309500000-reviewer-adopt-s1.glm-5.3.findings.md): the A1/A2/A4 mechanics are implemented and probe-verified, but found 2 P1 + 2 P2 + 2 P3: (P1-1) us