{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat src/cljc/dao/stream/ble.cljc; cat src/cljc/dao/stream/ble/links.cljc'","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.stream.ble\n  \"The raw Bluetooth layer of docs/design/dao.stream.ble.md: one radio\n   node exposed as dao.stream values. This layer carries bytes, peer\n   addresses and link facts and nothing else -- no decoding, retry,\n   ordering, dedup, fragmentation, reassembly, routing; each of those is\n   an interpreter above it, and the flooding mesh (dao.stream.ble.mesh)\n   is the first.\n\n   A radio node retains nothing, so it has no reader surface: a writer\n   handle (#{:writer :closable}) whose append! hands one addressed frame\n   to the radio, and a traffic stream, supplied by the composition, onto\n   which the host adapter deposits every received frame and every host\n   fact about the node and its links as one event. Readers hold their own\n   cursors on the traffic stream.\n\n   Binding is a host act, not create!, and the composition proceeds in\n   two explicit moves (section 3): the host seam (dao.stream.ble/dart)\n   takes {:identity id :deposit w :service-uuid u :max-frame-bytes n\n   :max-links n :announce-window-ms ms :now-ms f} -- a deposit writer and\n   nothing else, no function to invoke -- and returns at once {:send! f\n   :close! f}; the seam deposits :dao.stream.ble/bound with the node\n   identity on every host; the composition reads that event and calls\n   `writer` with the seam and the complete descriptor. A failed start\n   deposits :bind-failed and there is no writer.\n\n   A peer address is an opaque, link-scoped string -- Android reports a\n   MAC, iOS a per-local-device UUID -- and names one directional GATT\n   link as this radio's state observes it. No structure, no global\n   meaning, string equality: nothing above this layer may treat a peer\n   address as a node's name, which is why the mesh above floods (section\n   2 of the design).\n\n   A send failure is the caller's outcome when the host answers at call\n   time (:dao.stream/transport-error, clean: nothing was sent) and a\n   :dao.stream.ble/send-failed lifecycle event on the traffic stream for\n   its other observers -- always the event for a failure the host reports\n   only later, which is the channel this transport declares for an answer\n   it cannot give at call time (dao.stream.md, Writing). Excluded\n   append! outcomes: :full, because this layer holds no outbound queue\n   and a radio under pressure loses frames -- the medium's declared\n   nature, not a refusal; :refused, because no policy is composed in this\n   layer.\n\n   There is no :dao.stream/create entry. `attach!` on a BLE descriptor\n   off its host is :dao.stream/not-found; on its own host it resolves\n   only against nodes a composition chose to keep in its host-composed\n   attach closure -- `make-attacher` is that closure over a\n   composition-owned resolver, never a registry. Exposure is a real\n   hazard: a raw writer handle entered in a mirror table lets whoever\n   reaches it send arbitrary frames from this radio; no composition does\n   so without a gate on that entry (section 9).\"\n  (:require [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.base64 :as base64]))\n\n\n(def transport-type\n  \"The dao.stream/type of a bound radio node's descriptor.\"\n  :dao.stream/ble)\n\n\n(def default-service-uuid\n  \"The datom.world mesh profile's GATT service: a TX characteristic the\n   node notifies its frames on and an RX characteristic a central writes\n   its frames to. Composition data with this default; a composition that\n   changes it changes who can hear it.\"\n  \"7daf6c80-3f2a-4e11-9d47-1b2a3c4d5e6f\")\n\n\n(def default-tx-uuid\n  \"The mesh profile's TX characteristic (notify): this node's frames out\n   to a subscribed central.\"\n  \"7daf6c81-3f2a-4e11-9d47-1b2a3c4d5e6f\")\n\n\n(def default-rx-uuid\n  \"The mesh profile's RX characteristic (write): a central's frames in.\"\n  \"7daf6c82-3f2a-4e11-9d47-1b2a3c4d5e6f\")\n\n\n(def default-max-frame-bytes\n  \"The default symmetric frame budget: one notification payload under the\n   smallest ATT MTU hosts commonly negotiate (iOS has granted as little\n   as 185). A composition that observes a larger negotiated MTU may raise\n   it.\"\n  180)\n\n\n(def default-max-links\n  \"The default ceiling on concurrent GATT links: an iOS central holds\n   around ten.\"\n  8)\n\n\n(def default-announce-window-ms\n  \"The default discovery throttle: at most one peer-seen event per peer\n   per window, the latest RSSI winning.\"\n  2000)\n\n\n(defn- byte-length\n  [bs]\n  (bytes/length bs))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Values (section 2)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn peer-address?\n  \"True iff `s` is a peer address: a non-empty string. Opaque by design --\n   no structure is assigned and none is checked.\"\n  [s]\n  (and (string? s) (pos? (count s))))\n\n\n(defn node-id?\n  \"True iff `s` is a node identity: a non-empty string, composition\n   minted, never authenticated by this layer.\"\n  [s]\n  (and (string? s) (pos? (count s))))\n\n\n(defn outbound?\n  \"True iff `v` is one outbound value of section 2: a destination peer\n   address and the frame as strict Base64. The decoded length against the\n   budget is the writer's check, not this one's.\"\n  [v]\n  (and (map? v)\n       (peer-address? (:dao.stream.ble/destination v))\n       (base64/text? (:dao.stream.ble/bytes v))))\n\n\n(defn frame-event?\n  \"True iff `v` is one received frame as an event: exact bytes as strict\n   Base64, and the source peer the radio observed.\"\n  [v]\n  (and (map? v)\n       (peer-address? (:dao.stream.ble/source v))\n       (base64/text? (:dao.stream.ble/bytes v))))\n\n\n(def lifecycle-events\n  \"The lifecycle events this layer declares. A transport-owned event\n   keyword outside this set is not this layer's.\"\n  #{:dao.stream.ble/bound\n    :dao.stream.ble/bind-failed\n    :dao.stream.ble/peer-seen\n    :dao.stream.ble/peer-lost\n    :dao.stream.ble/link-up\n    :dao.stream.ble/link-down\n    :dao.stream.ble/send-failed\n    :dao.stream.ble/closed})\n\n\n(defn lifecycle-event?\n  \"True iff `v` is one host fact about the node itself or its links.\"\n  [v]\n  (and (map? v)\n       (node-id? (:dao.stream.ble/node v))\n       (contains? lifecycle-events (:dao.stream.ble/event v))))\n\n\n(defn bound-event\n  \"The bound lifecycle event: the node exists, with its identity.\"\n  [id self]\n  {:dao.stream.ble/node id\n   :dao.stream.ble/event :dao.stream.ble/bound\n   :dao.stream.ble/self self})\n\n\n(defn bind-failed-event\n  \"The failed-bind lifecycle event. There is no writer.\"\n  [id reason]\n  {:dao.stream.ble/node id\n   :dao.stream.ble/event :dao.stream.ble/bind-failed\n   :dao.stream.ble/reason reason})\n\n\n(defn peer-seen-event\n  \"One observed advertisement of the service UUID, throttled by the seam\n   to one event per peer per :announce-window-ms, latest RSSI winning.\"\n  [id peer rssi]\n  {:dao.stream.ble/node id\n   :dao.stream.ble/event :dao.stream.ble/peer-seen\n   :dao.stream.ble/peer peer\n   :dao.stream.ble/rssi rssi})\n\n\n(defn peer-lost-event\n  \"The peer-lost lifecycle event: a link to the peer went down. S1 seams\n   deposit it only from link loss, never from advertisement silence --\n   silence is not a fact a radio reports.\"\n  [id peer]\n  {:dao.stream.ble/node id\n   :dao.stream.ble/event :dao.stream.ble/peer-lost\n   :dao.stream.ble/peer peer})\n\n\n(defn link-up-event\n  \"The link-up lifecycle event: one directional GATT link exists, the\n   role named (:central connected out, :peripheral connected in).\"\n  [id peer direction]\n  {:dao.stream.ble/node id\n   :dao.stream.ble/event :dao.stream.ble/link-up\n   :dao.stream.ble/peer peer\n   :dao.stream.ble/direction direction})\n\n\n(defn link-down-event\n  \"The link-down lifecycle event: the directional link named by the peer\n   address is gone.\"\n  [id peer]\n  {:dao.stream.ble/node id\n   :dao.stream.ble/event :dao.stream.ble/link-down\n   :dao.stream.ble/peer peer})\n\n\n(defn send-failed-event\n  \"The send-failure lifecycle event: the channel for a send failure the\n   host could not answer at call time, and the observers' copy of one it\n   could.\"\n  [id peer reason]\n  {:dao.stream.ble/node id\n   :dao.stream.ble/event :dao.stream.ble/send-failed\n   :dao.stream.ble/peer peer\n   :dao.stream.ble/reason reason})\n\n\n(defn closed-event\n  \"The closed lifecycle event, deposited while the deposit writer still\n   admits it.\"\n  [id]\n  {:dao.stream.ble/node id\n   :dao.stream.ble/event :dao.stream.ble/closed})\n\n\n(defn frame-event\n  \"One received frame as an event: `bytes` encoded as Base64 so no host\n   byte array crosses onto a stream, with the source peer the radio\n   observed.\"\n  [id peer bytes]\n  {:dao.stream.ble/node id\n   :dao.stream.ble/source peer\n   :dao.stream.ble/bytes (base64/encode bytes)})\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The descriptor (section 3)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn descriptor?\n  \"{:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ble :dao.stream/identity id\n     :dao.stream.ble/self <node identity>}\n   The descriptor names the local radio node. It is reachability data in\n   the honest, reduced sense: a BLE node is reachable by radio proximity\n   and by advertising the service UUID, never by dialing the descriptor.\"\n  [d]\n  (and (map? d)\n       (= transport-type (:dao.stream/type d))\n       (node-id? (:dao.stream/identity d))\n       (node-id? (:dao.stream.ble/self d))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The writer handle (section 4)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- check-outbound\n  \"One outbound value of section 2 as either {:bytes bs} -- the decoded\n   frame, ready for the radio -- or {:refusal reason}: a malformed\n   destination, bytes that are not strict Base64, or a decoded length\n   over the budget. Nothing was sent for a refusal.\"\n  [v max-frame-bytes]\n  (cond\n    (not (map? v))\n    {:refusal \"not an outbound value\"}\n\n    (not (peer-address? (:dao.stream.ble/destination v)))\n    {:refusal \"malformed destination\"}\n\n    (not (base64/text? (:dao.stream.ble/bytes v)))\n    {:refusal \"bytes are not strict Base64\"}\n\n    :else\n    (let [bs (base64/decode (:dao.stream.ble/bytes v))]\n      (if (> (byte-length bs) max-frame-bytes)\n        {:refusal \"decoded length over :max-frame-bytes\"}\n        {:bytes bs}))))\n\n\n(deftype BLEWriter\n  [send-fn close-fn the-descriptor max-frame-bytes closed]\n\n  stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n\n  (descriptor\n    [_]\n    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n     :dao.stream/descriptor the-descriptor\n     :dao.stream/identity (:dao.stream/identity the-descriptor)})\n\n\n  stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n  (append!\n    [_ v]\n    (if @closed\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}\n      (let [checked (check-outbound v max-frame-bytes)]\n        (if-some [reason (:refusal checked)]\n          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-value\n           :dao.stream.ble/reason reason}\n          (let [r (try\n                    (send-fn (:dao.stream.ble/destination v)\n                             (:bytes checked))\n                    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n                      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n                       :dao.stream.ble/reason (str e)}))]\n            (if (and (map? r) (contains? r :dao.stream/outcome))\n              (if (#{:dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/transport-error\n                     :dao.stream/closed} (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n                r\n                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error})\n              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))))\n\n\n  stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n\n  (close!\n    [_]\n    (vreset! closed true)\n    (try (close-fn)\n         (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n           nil))\n    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))\n\n\n(defn writer\n  \"The composition's second move (section 3): the writer handle over a\n   bound `seam` ({:send! f :close! f}) and the complete `descriptor` the\n   bound event reported. `max-frame-bytes` is composition data, default\n   180, the same budget the seam was bound with.\"\n  ([seam descriptor]\n   (writer seam descriptor default-max-frame-bytes))\n  ([seam descriptor max-frame-bytes]\n   (when-not (and (map? seam)\n                  (fn? (:send! seam))\n                  (fn? (:close! seam)))\n     (throw (ex-info \"a dao.stream.ble seam is {:send! f :close! f}\"\n                     {:seam seam})))\n   (when-not (descriptor? descriptor)\n     (throw (ex-info \"not a dao.stream.ble descriptor\"\n                     {:descriptor descriptor})))\n   (BLEWriter. (:send! seam) (:close! seam) descriptor\n               (long max-frame-bytes) (volatile! false))))\n\n\n(defn make-attacher\n  \"The host-composed attach! closure over nodes a composition chose to\n   keep: `resolver` maps a node identity to its writer handle, or nil.\n   Attaching never creates, resolves nothing ambiently -- there is no\n   registry -- and the same handle is shared, not re-minted: a radio node\n   does not distinguish attachments.\"\n  [resolver]\n  (fn attach!\n    [descriptor]\n    (if-not (descriptor? descriptor)\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor}\n      (if-let [handle (resolver (:dao.stream/identity descriptor))]\n        (if (= (:dao.stream/identity descriptor)\n               (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor handle)))\n          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n           :dao.stream/handle handle}\n          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/not-found})\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/not-found}))))\n(ns dao.stream.ble.links\n  \"The host-free link state machine of docs/design/dao.stream.ble.md 6: a\n   seam's judgment is all link bookkeeping, and link bookkeeping is the\n   same on every host, so it lives here -- pure data over radio events --\n   and a host seam is a thin adapter that turns plugin streams into radio\n   events and returned actions into plugin calls. The dart seam holds no\n   policy of its own; a seam cannot drift from the tests that gate this\n   namespace.\n\n   Radio events are host-local vectors (never dao.stream values, never\n   deposited as such):\n\n     [:adv peer rssi]        an advertisement of the service UUID\n     [:link-up peer dir]     one directional GATT link exists\n                             (dir :central connected out, :peripheral in)\n     [:link-down peer]       that directional link is gone\n     [:link-failed peer]     a connect attempt ended without a link\n     [:frame peer bytes]     one frame arrived on that link\n     [:send-fail peer why]   the host reported a queued send as failed\n     [:radio-up self]        the radio started: advertising and scanning\n     [:radio-down why]       the radio stopped on its own (permissions,\n                             bluetooth off, suspension)\n     [:bind-failed why]      the radio never started\n\n   `handle-radio-event` answers {:state s' :deposits [...] :actions [...]}\n   : `:deposits` are dao.stream.ble values the caller appends to the\n   deposit writer in order, `:actions` are the radio calls the policy\n   owns: [:connect peer] -- an advertisement naming a peer with no link\n   and :max-links allowing, the medium's own repetition being the retry\n   cadence -- and nothing for a peer past the ceiling, whose\n   advertisement still deposits peer-seen. The ceiling counts\n   established links and pending dials both, and governs this seam's own\n   dials only: an inbound link always deposits.\n\n   `seam` is the generic adapter, host-free, that composes the machine\n   into the seam contract dao.stream.ble/writer consumes: it takes the\n   bind data and a radio map, appends every deposit to the deposit\n   writer in order, performs every action on the radio, and exposes\n   {:send! f :close! f :radio! f :state f} -- :send!/:close! are the\n   seam contract, :radio! is one radio event in, :state observes the\n   machine for tests. A send crosses the one directional GATT link the\n   peer address names; no link is the clean transport-error of section\n   4 plus a send-failed deposit; and both-directions redundancy -- two\n   nodes that each connect out to the other -- is a BLE fact the mesh's\n   dedup, not the seam's, eats (design 7): the machine cannot correlate\n   two opaque peer addresses, and does not pretend to.\"\n  (:require [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ble :as ble]))\n\n\n(def directions\n  \"The two roles one node can hold on one GATT link.\"\n  #{:central :peripheral})\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The pure state machine\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn initial-state\n  \"The machine's state over the bind data: `:now-ms` is the clock the\n   discovery throttle reads, (f) -> integer milliseconds -- a host seam\n   supplies the host clock, tests supply a deterministic one. The clock\n   is the seam's own operational fact; no protocol state below the seam\n   reads it.\"\n  [{:keys [identity max-links announce-window-ms max-frame-bytes now-ms]}]\n  (when-not (ble/node-id? identity)\n    (throw (ex-info \"a dao.stream.ble seam needs :identity, a node id\"\n                    {:identity identity})))\n  (when-not (fn? now-ms)\n    (throw (ex-info \"a dao.stream.ble seam needs :now-ms, a clock\"\n                    {:now-ms now-ms})))\n  {:identity identity\n   :max-links (or max-links ble/default-max-links)\n   :announce-window-ms (or announce-window-ms\n                           ble/default-announce-window-ms)\n   :max-frame-bytes (or max-frame-bytes ble/default-max-frame-bytes)\n   :now-ms now-ms\n   :links {}\n   :connecting #{}\n   :announced {}\n   :closed? false})\n\n\n(defn- link-direction\n  \"The direction last reported for the link `peer` names. One peer\n   address is one entry: a platform that reports both directions of one\n   pairing under one address re-marks the entry's direction, and the\n   first [:link-down ...] for that address drops it.\"\n  [state peer]\n  (:direction (get (:links state) peer)))\n\n\n(defn- throttle-deposit?\n  \"True iff `state` owes `peer` a peer-seen deposit now: no window is\n   open, or its window has elapsed. The first advertisement always\n   deposits.\"\n  [state peer]\n  (if-some [since (get (:announced state) peer)]\n    (>= ((:now-ms state)) (+ since (:announce-window-ms state)))\n    true))\n\n\n(defn- note-announced\n  [state peer]\n  (assoc-in state [:announced peer] ((:now-ms state))))\n\n\n(defn- link-count-ok?\n  \"The ceiling counts established links and pending connects both: a\n   burst of advertisements from different peers issues at most\n   :max-links dials, whatever the radio does with them.\"\n  [state]\n  (< (+ (count (:links state)) (count (:connecting state)))\n     (:max-links state)))\n\n\n(defn- prune-announced\n  \"Announcement windows older than :announce-window-ms are dropped, so\n   a scanner seeing rotating random addresses does not grow the map\n   without bound. Pure: answers the pruned state.\"\n  [state]\n  (let [now ((:now-ms state))\n        horizon (- now (:announce-window-ms state))]\n    (assoc state :announced\n           (into {} (filter (fn [[_ since]] (>= since horizon)))\n                 (:announced state)))))\n\n\n(defn- answer\n  \"The machine's answer shape: the next state, the deposits to append in\n   order, the actions to perform in order.\"\n  [state deposits actions]\n  {:state state :deposits (vec deposits) :actions (vec actions)})\n\n\n(defn handle-radio-event\n  \"One radio event in, the machine's answer out. Total: an event the\n   machine does not know is answered with the state unchanged, no\n   deposits, no actions -- a newer radio, not a defect.\"\n  [state ev]\n  (let [[kind peer arg] ev]\n    (if (:closed? state)\n      (answer state [] [])\n      (case kind\n        :radio-up\n        (answer state [(ble/bound-event (:identity state) peer)] [])\n\n        :bind-failed\n        (answer state [(ble/bind-failed-event (:identity state) peer)] [])\n\n        :radio-down\n        ;; The radio stopped on its own: every live link is lost, and the\n        ;; node this composition held is observably gone (dao.stream.md,\n        ;; Surfaces). Sends through the writer answer transport-error\n        ;; from here on -- no links -- until the composition re-binds.\n        (let [peers (vec (keys (:links state)))]\n          (answer (assoc state :links {} :connecting #{} :announced {})\n                  (into [(ble/closed-event (:identity state))]\n                        (map (fn [p]\n                               (ble/link-down-event (:identity state) p)))\n                        peers)\n                  [[:stop-radio]]))\n\n        :adv\n        ;; One observed advertisement of the service UUID. The throttle\n        ;; owes at most one peer-seen per peer per :announce-window-ms,\n        ;; latest RSSI winning; the connect policy rides the same window,\n        ;; so the medium's own repetition is the retry cadence.\n        (let [s (prune-announced state)\n              owes? (throttle-deposit? s peer)\n              s (if owes? (note-announced s peer) s)\n              deposits (if owes?\n                         [(ble/peer-seen-event (:identity state) peer arg)]\n                         [])\n              actions (if (and owes?\n                               (not (contains? (:links state) peer))\n                               (not (contains? (:connecting s) peer))\n                               (link-count-ok? s))\n                        [[:connect peer]]\n                        [])\n              s (if (seq actions)\n                  (update s :connecting conj peer)\n                  s)]\n          (answer s deposits actions))\n\n        ;; The ceiling of section 6 governs this seam's own dials, not\n        ;; what the OS accepts on its side: an inbound link always\n        ;; deposits, whatever :max-links says.\n        :link-up\n        (answer (-> state\n                    (assoc-in [:links peer] {:direction arg})\n                    (update :connecting disj peer))\n                [(ble/link-up-event (:identity state) peer arg)]\n                [])\n\n        ;; A link whose peer address the machine never saw come up is a\n        ;; radio fact about nothing this node holds -- the stale\n        ;; duplicate of a teardown already processed. It deposits\n        ;; nothing: a never-held link is not a lost one.\n        :link-down\n        (if (contains? (:links state) peer)\n          (answer (-> state\n                      (update :links dissoc peer)\n                      (update :connecting disj peer))\n                  [(ble/link-down-event (:identity state) peer)\n                   (ble/peer-lost-event (:identity state) peer)]\n                  [])\n          (answer (update state :connecting disj peer) [] []))\n\n        ;; A connect attempt ended without a link: no deposit -- the next\n        ;; advertisement window retries, and a never-up link is not a\n        ;; lost one.\n        :link-failed\n        (answer (update state :connecting disj peer) [] [])\n\n        :frame\n        ;; The :max-frame-bytes drop is protocol validation below the\n        ;; transform: an inbound frame over the budget is never\n        ;; deposited, the same symmetric budget design 4 refuses at\n        ;; append!.\n        (if (> (bytes/length arg) (:max-frame-bytes state))\n          (answer state [] [])\n          (answer state\n                  [(ble/frame-event (:identity state) peer arg)]\n                  []))\n\n        :send-fail\n        (answer state\n                [(ble/send-failed-event (:identity state) peer arg)]\n                [])\n\n        (answer state [] [])))))\n\n\n(defn send!\n  \"One frame toward `peer`, decoded host bytes, over the one directional\n   GATT link that peer address names: either an outcome and a\n   [:send-frame ...] action, or the clean transport-error of section 4\n   plus a send-failed deposit when no such link exists at this moment.\n   \\\"No link\\\" is a normal BLE fact -- links come and go with proximity\n   -- and is not distinguished from any other failure; the writer of a\n   flooding mesh does not retry it, because the mesh's redundancy is the\n   retry.\"\n  [state peer bs]\n  (cond\n    (:closed? state)\n    {:state state\n     :outcome {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}\n     :deposits [] :actions []}\n\n    (not (ble/peer-address? peer))\n    {:state state\n     :outcome {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n               :dao.stream.ble/reason \"malformed destination\"}\n     :deposits [(ble/send-failed-event (:identity state) peer\n                                       \"malformed destination\")]\n     :actions []}\n\n    (nil? (link-direction state peer))\n    {:state state\n     :outcome {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n               :dao.stream.ble/reason \"no link to peer\"}\n     :deposits [(ble/send-failed-event (:identity state) peer\n                                       \"no link to peer\")]\n     :actions []}\n\n    :else\n    {:state state\n     :outcome {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}\n     :deposits []\n     :actions [[:send-frame peer bs]]}))\n\n\n(defn close!\n  \"The close path: the node stops advertising, scanning and serving, and\n   is observably gone. Every live link is lost with it, and each is\n   deposited as a link-down first -- the mesh above learns its neighbors\n   from those events, and a link fact the reader held must not outlive\n   the reader's evidence for it (design 5). Idempotent: a closed node's\n   close answers without deposits or actions.\"\n  [state]\n  (if (:closed? state)\n    (answer state [] [])\n    (answer (assoc state :closed? true :links {} :connecting #{})\n            (into [(ble/closed-event (:identity state))]\n                  (map (fn [p] (ble/link-down-event (:identity state) p)))\n                  (keys (:links state)))\n            [[:stop-radio]])))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The generic adapter: one seam, any radio\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- append-deposits!\n  \"Every deposit onto the deposit writer, in order, each appended even if\n   the one before it answered non-ok -- the deposit writer is an evicting\n   ring by contract and never refuses (design 5). Total even if the\n   composition behind it is broken.\"\n  [deposit deposits]\n  (doseq [ev deposits]\n    (try (stream/append! deposit ev)\n         (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n\n\n(defn seam\n  \"The generic adapter (design 6): the machine composed into the seam\n   contract `dao.stream.ble/writer` consumes, over a `radio` map the\n   host supplies:\n\n     {:perform! (fn [action])}   machine -> radio: [:connect peer],\n                                 [:send-frame peer bytes], [:stop-radio]\n\n   and answers {:send! f :close! f :radio! f :state f}: `:send!`/\n   `:close!` are the seam contract (bind data in, those two out, deposits\n   flowing to `:deposit` only); `:radio!` is the adapter's one entry, one\n   radio event in; `:state` observes the machine, for tests. `:send!`\n   hands the frame to the radio and answers `ok` -- it asserts nothing\n   about the air -- and a failure the host reports later arrives as a\n   [:send-fail ...] radio event, the send-failed channel of design 4.\n   The radio's own send failures are deposited; they are not retried.\"\n  [{:keys [identity deposit max-frame-bytes max-links announce-window-ms\n           now-ms radio]}]\n  (when-not (and (map? radio) (fn? (:perform! radio)))\n    (throw (ex-info \"a dao.stream.ble seam needs a radio with :perform!\"\n                    {:radio radio})))\n  (let [state (atom (initial-state\n                     {:identity identity\n                      :max-links max-links\n                      :announce-window-ms announce-window-ms\n                      :max-frame-bytes max-frame-bytes\n                      :now-ms now-ms}))\n        run! (fn [a]\n               (reset! state (:state a))\n               (append-deposits! deposit (:deposits a))\n               (doseq [action (:actions a)] ((:perform! radio) action)))]\n    {:send!\n     (fn [peer bs]\n       (let [a (send! @state peer bs)]\n         (run! a)\n         (:outcome a)))\n     :close!\n     (fn []\n       (run! (close! @state))\n       nil)\n     :radio!\n     (fn [ev]\n       (run! (handle-radio-event @state ev))\n       nil)\n     :state\n     (fn [] @state)}))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
