{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files collab orchestrator-logs archive | rg -- '-ble[-./_]'; rg -n 'ble|BLE' docs/agents/build-n-test.md deps.edn bb.edn; cat test/dao/stream/ble_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"rg: archive: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nbb.edn:50:  {:doc \"J5 acceptance: one Python session through the JVM and jolt REPL entry points with the standard catalog (output equal line for line), the multiline probe sequence, and the unavailable-library REPL legs (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\nbb.edn:55:  {:doc \"J5b: the native Python parser's budget (input 4 MiB; in-parser guards: 8192 rule frames, 4096 SLL lookahead links, 256 full-LL links, on a 16 MiB parse thread): the review's repros, at/over per shape against the predicted table, 10x the old crash depths, the JVM's packets (incl. a 20,000-deep 1+ tree), the old crash depths in children on the jolt thread, injected C++ faults, the abort-is-a-failure property, lifecycle and unavailable-library legs. Args select legs: budget below crash inject abort unavailable (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\nbb.edn:142:  {:doc \"J2: every applicable pure suite (test/dao/host, jing, data, space, portable stream, yin/vm) under jolt, one namespace per process through src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj, fast and ^:slow alike (Q3), nonzero exit on any failure; excluded suites are printed and recorded with reason/capability/owner\"\nbb.edn:162:  {:doc \"J2: the jolt-vs-JVM per-namespace count table from build/j2-logs/{core,jvm}-summary.edn; runs nothing\"\nbb.edn:309:  test:slow:cljs {:doc \"Node: only namespaces with dao.test-slow/guard, bodies enabled (DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\nbb.edn:320:  test:slow:cljd {:doc \"Dart: only generated tests of namespaces with dao.test-slow/guard, bodies enabled (DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\ndeps.edn:90:           ;; listed for audited portable namespaces only (its JVM namespaces\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:30:# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:145:`test:routed <changed-files...>` applies this priority table to the whole change\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:174:executable examples or validate documentation links.\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:188:serialization rule. G1, full post-merge `bb test` (G3), applicable slow G4,\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:191:available. **Never run the slow tier, `bb test:all`, or `nightly.clj` on the\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:196:workers, shiva comparable). Do not run another lane set concurrently on the\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:214:ensure this dependency too. Direct `npm ci` is still available.\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:219:not a shared artifact store: never share mutable `build/`, `lib/`, `target/` or\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:222:does not make overlapping builds and tests safe. Peer executables and shadow\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:336:different namespaces share an isolate per shard. Failures stay attributable:\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:554:avoidable\"). The laptop additionally never runs the slow tier or the nightly\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:585:1. **`npm install`** — the Node tests require npm deps (`@noble/hashes` was\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:709:  `SO_REUSEADDR` for UDP**, so a second bind to a port a reuse-enabled socket already\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:742:  touches), one JVM per namespace, plus one cheap portable lane (Node)\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:799:are installed and usable **on the remote hosts themselves**, not only from the\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:819:   (role template, bounded file ownership, deliverable path), just executing\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:834:jolt canonical-fixes verification ran there); `glm` reported available by the\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:851:This ensures code is testable by design and implementation matches actual requirements.\n(ns dao.stream.ble-test\n  \"Portable, host-free tests for dao.stream.ble\n   (docs/design/dao.stream.ble.md): the value shapes of section 2, the\n   peer-address rule, the descriptor of section 3, and every\n   append!/close! outcome of the writer handle of section 4 over a\n   scripted host seam. The seam contract itself is what the link\n   machine's tests (dao.stream.ble.links-test) drive and the sim\n   exercises end to end; everything here proves the portable layer's own\n   decisions without a host.\"\n\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.base64 :as base64]\n            [dao.stream.ble :as ble])\n  #?(:cljd (:import [\"dart:typed_data\" Uint8List])))\n\n\n(def ^:private peer \"peer-1\")\n(def ^:private node-id \"ble-node\")\n\n\n(defn- octets->bytes\n  \"One octet payload as host bytes, the only host dependence here.\"\n  [octets]\n  #?(:cljd (Uint8List.fromList (vec octets))\n     :clj (byte-array (mapv unchecked-byte octets))\n     :cljs (js/Uint8Array.from (to-array (vec octets)))))\n\n\n(defn- octets-of\n  \"Any byte payload as a vector of unsigned octets, the one shape that\n   compares equal on every host.\"\n  [bs]\n  (mapv (fn [b] (bit-and 0xff (int b))) (seq bs)))\n\n\n(defn- outbound\n  \"One outbound value of section 2.\"\n  [p octets]\n  {:dao.stream.ble/destination p\n   :dao.stream.ble/bytes (base64/encode (octets->bytes octets))})\n\n\n(defn- descriptor\n  ([]\n   {:dao.stream/type ble/transport-type\n    :dao.stream/identity node-id\n    :dao.stream.ble/self node-id})\n  ([self]\n   {:dao.stream/type ble/transport-type\n    :dao.stream/identity node-id\n    :dao.stream.ble/self self}))\n\n\n(defn- writer-over\n  \"The writer handle over a scripted seam and the descriptor.\"\n  ([seam] (ble/writer seam (descriptor)))\n  ([seam max] (ble/writer seam (descriptor) max)))\n\n\n(defn- scripted-seam\n  \"A fake host seam: `:sends` records every frame as [peer bytes];\n   `:fail` answers the next n sends with the clean transport-error of\n   section 4 (the deposit side is the composition's, which the links\n   tests drive); `:closes` counts close!s.\"\n  [& {:keys [fail]}]\n  (let [sends (atom [])\n        fail (atom (or fail 0))\n        closes (atom 0)\n        seam {:send!\n              (fn [p bs]\n                (if (pos? @fail)\n                  (do (swap! fail dec)\n                      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n                       :dao.stream.ble/reason \"scripted refusal\"})\n                  (do (swap! sends conj [p bs])\n                      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})))\n              :close! (fn [] (swap! closes inc) nil)}]\n    {:seam seam :sends sends :fail fail :closes closes}))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Section 2: values\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(deftest peer-addresses-are-opaque-nonempty-strings\n  (testing \"any non-empty string is a peer address\"\n    (is (ble/peer-address? \"AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF\"))\n    (is (ble/peer-address? \"6E400001-B5A3-F393-E0A9-E50E24DCCA9E\"))\n    (is (ble/peer-address? \"peer-1\")))\n  (testing \"no structure is assigned and none is checked\"\n    (is (ble/peer-address? \" not an address at all \")))\n  (testing \"empty and non-string destinations are malformed\"\n    (is (not (ble/peer-address? \"\")))\n    (is (not (ble/peer-address? nil)))\n    (is (not (ble/peer-address? 42)))))\n\n\n(deftest outbound-and-frame-values\n  (let [good (outbound peer [1 2 3])]\n    (testing \"an outbound value of section 2\"\n      (is (ble/outbound? good)))\n    (testing \"a malformed destination or non-Base64 bytes is not\"\n      (is (not (ble/outbound? {:dao.stream.ble/destination \"\"\n                               :dao.stream.ble/bytes (:dao.stream.ble/bytes good)})))\n      (is (not (ble/outbound? (assoc good :dao.stream.ble/bytes \"not base64!\")))))\n    (testing \"a frame event of section 2\"\n      (is (ble/frame-event?\n           (ble/frame-event node-id peer (octets->bytes [9 8 7]))))\n      (is (not (ble/frame-event?\n                (assoc (ble/frame-event node-id peer (octets->bytes [9]))\n                       :dao.stream.ble/bytes \"ab cd\")))))))\n\n\n(deftest lifecycle-events-carry-the-node-and-a-declared-event\n  (let [id node-id]\n    (doseq [ev [(ble/bound-event id id)\n                (ble/bind-failed-event id \"denied\")\n                (ble/peer-seen-event id peer -60)\n                (ble/peer-lost-event id peer)\n                (ble/link-up-event id peer :central)\n                (ble/link-down-event id peer)\n                (ble/send-failed-event id peer \"no link\")\n                (ble/closed-event id)]]\n      (is (ble/lifecycle-event? ev)))\n    (testing \"an undeclared event keyword is not this layer's\"\n      (is (not (ble/lifecycle-event?\n                {:dao.stream.ble/node id\n                 :dao.stream.ble/event :dao.stream.ble/something-new}))))\n    (testing \"a frame event is not a lifecycle event and the reverse\"\n      (is (not (ble/lifecycle-event?\n                (ble/frame-event id peer (octets->bytes [1])))))\n      (is (not (ble/frame-event? (ble/closed-event id)))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Section 3: the descriptor\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(deftest descriptor-names-the-local-node\n  (is (ble/descriptor? (descriptor)))\n  (testing \"self may differ from the composition's id\"\n    (is (ble/descriptor? (descriptor \"aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff\")))\n    (is (= \"aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff\"\n           (:dao.stream.ble/self (descriptor \"aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff\")))))\n  (testing \"the type, identity and self are all required\"\n    (is (not (ble/descriptor? {})))\n    (is (not (ble/descriptor? (dissoc (descriptor) :dao.stream/identity))))\n    (is (not (ble/descriptor? (dissoc (descriptor) :dao.stream.ble/self))))\n    (is (not (ble/descriptor?\n              (assoc (descriptor) :dao.stream/type :dao.stream/datagram))))\n    (is (not (ble/descriptor?\n              (assoc (descriptor) :dao.stream.ble/self \"\"))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Section 4: the writer handle\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(deftest append-hands-one-frame-to-the-seam\n  (let [s (scripted-seam)\n        w (writer-over (:seam s))\n        r (stream/append! w (outbound peer [1 2 3]))]\n    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n    (is (= [[peer [1 2 3]]]\n           (mapv (fn [[p bs]] [p (octets-of bs)]) @(:sends s))))))\n\n\n(deftest malformed-outbounds-are-invalid-value-and-never-sent\n  (let [s (scripted-seam)\n        w (writer-over (:seam s) 8)]\n    (testing \"a malformed destination\"\n      (let [r (stream/append! w (assoc (outbound peer [1]) :dao.stream.ble/destination \"\"))]\n        (is (= :dao.stream/invalid-value (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n        (is (string? (:dao.stream.ble/reason r)))))\n    (testing \"bytes that are not strict Base64\"\n      (let [r (stream/append! w (assoc (outbound peer [1]) :dao.stream.ble/bytes \"ab cd\"))]\n        (is (= :dao.stream/invalid-value (:dao.stream/outcome r)))))\n    (testing \"a decoded length over the budget\"\n      (let [r (stream/append! w (outbound peer [1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9]))]\n        (is (= :dao.stream/invalid-value (:dao.stream/outcome r)))))\n    (testing \"not a map at all\"\n      (is (= :dao.stream/invalid-value (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! w 42)))))\n    (testing \"nothing was sent\"\n      (is (empty? @(:sends s))))))\n\n\n(deftest exactly-at-the-budget-is-accepted\n  (let [s (scripted-seam)\n        w (writer-over (:seam s) 3)]\n    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! w (outbound peer [1 2 3])))))\n    (is (= 1 (count @(:sends s))))))\n\n\n(deftest synchronous-send-failures-are-clean\n  (let [s (scripted-seam :fail 2)\n        w (writer-over (:seam s))]\n    (dotimes [_ 2]\n      (let [r (stream/append! w (outbound peer [1]))]\n        (is (= :dao.stream/transport-error (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n        (is (= \"scripted refusal\" (:dao.stream.ble/reason r)))))\n    (testing \"the seam was never handed the failed frames\"\n      (is (empty? @(:sends s))))))\n\n\n(deftest close-answers-ok-tears-down-and-is-idempotent\n  (let [s (scripted-seam)\n        w (writer-over (:seam s))]\n    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/close! w))))\n    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/close! w))))\n    (testing \"each close reaches the seam, which tolerates the repeat\"\n      (is (= 2 @(:closes s))))\n    (testing \"a closed handle appends closed and sends nothing\"\n      (is (= :dao.stream/closed\n             (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! w (outbound peer [1])))))\n      (is (empty? @(:sends s))))\n    (testing \"the descriptor still answers ok after close\"\n      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/descriptor w)))))))\n\n\n(deftest descriptor-answers-identity-and-reachability\n  (let [s (scripted-seam)\n        w (writer-over (:seam s))\n        r (stream/descriptor w)]\n    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n    (is (= node-id (:dao.stream/identity r)))\n    (is (= (descriptor) (:dao.stream/descriptor r)))\n    (testing \"the identity projection and the descriptor's agree\"\n      (is (= (:dao.stream/identity (:dao.stream/descriptor r))\n             (:dao.stream/identity r))))))\n\n\n(deftest bad-seams-and-descriptors-are-assembly-defects\n  (testing \"a seam without send!/close! throws before any operation\"\n    (is (thrown? #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs js/Error)\n                 (ble/writer {:send! (fn [_p _bs])} (descriptor))))\n    (is (thrown? #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs js/Error)\n                 (ble/writer nil (descriptor)))))\n  (testing \"a non-descriptor throws\"\n    (is (thrown? #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs js/Error)\n                 (ble/writer (:seam (scripted-seam)) {:dao.stream/type :nope})))))\n\n\n(deftest a-seam-answer-is-taken-at-its-outcome\n  (testing \"an outcome map outside the declared set answers transport-error\"\n    (let [seam {:send! (fn [_p _bs] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/not-mine})\n                :close! (fn [])}\n          w (writer-over seam)]\n      (is (= :dao.stream/transport-error\n             (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! w (outbound peer [1])))))))\n  (testing \"a seam answering nothing at all is ok -- the frame was handed over\"\n    (let [seam {:send! (fn [_p _bs] :whatever)\n                :close! (fn [])}\n          w (writer-over seam)]\n      (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n             (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! w (outbound peer [1]))))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Section 3: attach!\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(deftest attach-resolves-only-what-the-composition-kept\n  (let [s (scripted-seam)\n        w (writer-over (:seam s))\n        attach! (ble/make-attacher {node-id w})]\n    (testing \"the kept node's descriptor attaches to the same handle\"\n      (let [r (attach! (descriptor))]\n        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n        (is (identical? w (:dao.stream/handle r)))))\n    (testing \"a malformed descriptor is invalid-descriptor\"\n      (is (= :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor (:dao.stream/outcome (attach! {})))))\n    (testing \"a node the composition did not keep is not-found\"\n      (is (= :dao.stream/not-found\n             (:dao.stream/outcome\n              (attach! (assoc (descriptor) :dao.stream/identity \"other\"))))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The default composition data of section 3\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(deftest defaults\n  (is (re-matches #\"[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}\"\n                  ble/default-service-uuid))\n  (is (re-matches #\"[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}\"\n                  ble/default-tx-uuid))\n  (is (re-matches #\"[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}\"\n                  ble/default-rx-uuid))\n  (is (= 180 ble/default-max-frame-bytes))\n  (is (= 8 ble/default-max-links))\n  (is (= 2000 ble/default-announce-window-ms)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/dao/stream/ble/dart_test.cljd; sed -n '1,250p' test/dao/stream/ble/links_test.cljc; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest|\"'^'\"\\\\(defn' test/dao/stream/ble/mesh_test.cljc; sed -n '350,510p' docs/design/dao.stream.ble.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/dao/stream/ble/dart_test.cljd; sed -n '1,250p' test/dao/stream/ble/links_test.cljc; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest|\"'^'\"\\\\(defn' test/dao/stream/ble/mesh_test.cljc; sed -n '350,510p' docs/design/dao.stream.ble.md\"","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.stream.ble.dart-test\n  \"The Flutter seam (dao.stream.ble/dart) in the flutter_test sandbox,\n   where every plugin method channel is unregistered: each platform\n   call completes with null or fails, and none of it is a device. What\n   the sandbox can prove is the seam contract's shape and the laws that\n   hold without a radio -- send with no link, close idempotent, every\n   deposited event inside the declared set. The compile of this\n   namespace is also the compile check of the plugin interop; scans,\n   links and frames need real radios and are the seam's device-test\n   plan.\"\n\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [\"dart:core\" :as core]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ble :as ble]\n            [dao.stream.ble.dart :as dart]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer])\n  (:import [\"dart:typed_data\" Uint8List]))\n\n\n(defn- ring\n  [capacity]\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n                         ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity})))\n\n\n(defn- values\n  [h]\n  (loop [c (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h stream/anchor-oldest))\n         acc []]\n    (let [r (stream/next h c)]\n      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc (:dao.stream/value r)))\n        acc))))\n\n\n(deftest the-seam-contract-holds-without-a-radio\n  (let [traffic (ring 64)\n        seam (dart/bind! {:identity \"ble-test-node\"\n                          :deposit traffic\n                          :now-ms #(.-millisecondsSinceEpoch\n                                    (core/DateTime.now))})]\n    (testing \"the bind move answers the seam contract at once\"\n      (is (fn? (:send! seam)))\n      (is (fn? (:close! seam)))\n      (is (fn? (:radio! seam)))\n      (is (fn? (:state seam))))\n    (testing \"a send with no link is the clean transport-error\"\n      (is (= :dao.stream/transport-error\n             (:dao.stream/outcome\n              ((:send! seam) \"peer-nowhere\" (Uint8List.fromList [1]))))))\n    (testing \"every deposited event is one of the declared lifecycle events\"\n      (is (every? #(contains? ble/lifecycle-events %)\n                  (->> (values traffic)\n                       (filter ble/lifecycle-event?)\n                       (mapv :dao.stream.ble/event)))))\n    (testing \"close answers ok and is idempotent, and deposits closed\"\n      ((:close! seam))\n      ((:close! seam))\n      (is (= :dao.stream.ble/closed\n             (:dao.stream.ble/event (last (values traffic))))))))\n(ns dao.stream.ble.links-test\n  \"Host-free tests for the link state machine and the generic adapter\n   (docs/design/dao.stream.ble.md 6): the discovery throttle and the\n   connect policy, the link and frame deposits, the symmetric frame\n   budget, the send rule, close, radio-down, and the seam wiring -- every\n   deposit appended to the deposit writer in order, every action\n   performed in order, and no policy anywhere else. The machine is pure,\n   so every law is stated over explicit states and explicit clocks.\"\n\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.base64 :as base64]\n            [dao.stream.ble :as ble]\n            [dao.stream.ble.links :as links]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer])\n  #?(:cljd (:import [\"dart:typed_data\" Uint8List])))\n\n\n(def ^:private peer \"peer-1\")\n(def ^:private peer-b \"peer-2\")\n\n\n(defn- octets->bytes\n  [octets]\n  #?(:cljd (Uint8List.fromList (vec octets))\n     :clj (byte-array (mapv unchecked-byte octets))\n     :cljs (js/Uint8Array.from (to-array (vec octets)))))\n\n\n(defn- octets-of\n  [bs]\n  (mapv (fn [b] (bit-and 0xff (int b))) (seq bs)))\n\n\n(defn- state\n  \"The machine over a controllable clock: `!now` is an atom of integer\n   milliseconds.\"\n  [!now & {:keys [max-links announce-window-ms max-frame-bytes]}]\n  (links/initial-state\n   {:identity \"ble-node\"\n    :max-links max-links\n    :announce-window-ms announce-window-ms\n    :max-frame-bytes max-frame-bytes\n    :now-ms (fn [] @!now)}))\n\n\n(defn- events-of\n  [answer]\n  (mapv :dao.stream.ble/event (:deposits answer)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The discovery throttle and the connect policy\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(deftest first-advertisement-deposits-and-connects\n  (let [!now (atom 1000)\n        s (state !now)\n        {:keys [state deposits actions]}\n        (links/handle-radio-event s [:adv peer -60])]\n    (is (= [:dao.stream.ble/peer-seen] (events-of {:deposits deposits})))\n    (is (= peer (:dao.stream.ble/peer (first deposits))))\n    (is (= -60 (:dao.stream.ble/rssi (first deposits))))\n    (is (= [[:connect peer]] actions))\n    (testing \"the window opened\"\n      (is (contains? (:announced state) peer)))))\n\n\n(deftest advertisements-within-the-window-deposit-nothing\n  (let [!now (atom 1000)\n        s (state !now :announce-window-ms 2000)\n        s1 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s [:adv peer -60]))\n        s2 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s1 [:adv peer -70]))]\n    (is (= [] (events-of (links/handle-radio-event s2 [:adv peer -80]))))\n    (testing \"past the window, the latest RSSI wins\"\n      (swap! !now + 2001)\n      (let [{:keys [deposits]} (links/handle-radio-event s2 [:adv peer -80])]\n        (is (= [:dao.stream.ble/peer-seen] (events-of {:deposits deposits})))\n        (is (= -80 (:dao.stream.ble/rssi (first deposits))))))))\n\n\n(deftest a-linked-peer-is-not-reconnected\n  (let [!now (atom 1000)\n        s (state !now)\n        s1 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s [:adv peer -60]))\n        s2 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s1 [:link-up peer :central]))]\n    (testing \"inside the window the advertisement deposits nothing\"\n      (is (= [] (events-of (links/handle-radio-event s2 [:adv peer -70])))))\n    (testing \"past the window the latest RSSI is deposited, and the peer\n              is not reconnected -- it is linked\"\n      (swap! !now + 2001)\n      (let [{:keys [deposits actions]}\n            (links/handle-radio-event s2 [:adv peer -80])]\n        (is (= [:dao.stream.ble/peer-seen] (events-of {:deposits deposits})))\n        (is (= -80 (:dao.stream.ble/rssi (first deposits))))\n        (is (= [] actions))))))\n\n\n(deftest the-ceiling-refuses-nothing-and-connects-nothing\n  (let [!now (atom 1000)\n        s (state !now :max-links 1)\n        s1 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s [:adv peer -60]))\n        s2 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s1 [:link-up peer :central]))\n        a3 (links/handle-radio-event s2 [:adv peer-b -60])\n        st3 (:state a3)\n        {:keys [deposits actions]} a3]\n    (is (= [:dao.stream.ble/peer-seen] (events-of {:deposits deposits})))\n    (is (= [] actions))\n    (testing \"the first peer's dial is pending: the ceiling counts it\"\n      (is (contains? (:connecting s1) peer)))\n    (testing \"the composition that wants more links raises :max-links,\n              and the peer's next advertisement connects\"\n      (let [s3 (assoc st3 :max-links 2)]\n        (swap! !now + 2001)\n        (let [{:keys [actions]}\n              (links/handle-radio-event s3 [:adv peer-b -60])]\n          (is (= [[:connect peer-b]] actions)))))))\n\n\n(deftest a-dialing-peer-is-not-dialed-again\n  (let [!now (atom 1000)\n        s (state !now)\n        s1 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s [:adv peer -60]))]\n    (swap! !now + 2001)\n    (testing \"the dial is already out; the next window dials nothing\"\n      (is (= [] (:actions (links/handle-radio-event s1 [:adv peer -60])))))\n    (testing \"a failed attempt frees the slot; the next window dials again\"\n      (let [s2 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s1 [:link-failed peer]))]\n        (is (empty? (:connecting s2)))\n        (swap! !now + 2001)\n        (is (= [[:connect peer]]\n               (:actions (links/handle-radio-event s2 [:adv peer -60]))))))))\n\n\n(deftest an-inbound-link-always-deposits-whatever-the-ceiling\n  (let [!now (atom 1000)\n        s (state !now :max-links 1)\n        s1 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s [:adv peer -60]))\n        s2 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s1 [:link-up peer :central]))\n        s3 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s2 [:link-up peer-b :peripheral]))\n        a4 (links/handle-radio-event s3 [:link-up \"peer-3\" :peripheral])]\n    (is (= [:dao.stream.ble/link-up] (events-of a4)))\n    (is (= 2 (count (:links s3))))\n    (is (= 3 (count (:links (:state a4)))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Links and frames\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(deftest link-up-and-down-deposit-and-track-direction\n  (let [!now (atom 0)\n        s (state !now)\n        s1 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s [:link-up peer :central]))\n        s2 (:state (links/handle-radio-event s1 [:link-up peer-b :peripheral]))]\n    (is (= :central (:direction (get (:links s1) peer))))\n    (is (= :peripheral (:direction (get (:links s2) peer-b))))\n    (is (= 2 (count (:links s2))))\n    (let [{:keys [deposits]} (links/handle-radio-event s2 [:link-down peer])]\n      (is (= [:dao.stream.ble/link-down :dao.stream.ble/peer-lost]\n             (events-of {:deposits deposits}))))\n    (is (= 1 (count (:links (:state (links/handle-radio-event\n                                     s2 [:link-down peer]))))))))\n\n\n(deftest a-link-down-for-an-unknown-peer-deposits-nothing\n  (let [!now (atom 0)\n        s (state !now)\n        {:keys [deposits actions state]}\n        (links/handle-radio-event s [:link-down peer])]\n    (is (= [] deposits))\n    (is (= [] actions))\n    (is (= s state))))\n\n\n(deftest close-deposits-a-link-down-for-every-live-link\n  (let [!now (atom 0)\n        s (:state (links/handle-radio-event (state !now) [:link-up peer :central]))\n        s (:state (links/handle-radio-event s [:link-up peer-b :peripheral]))\n        {:keys [deposits actions]}\n        (links/close! s)]\n    (is (= [:dao.stream.ble/closed\n            :dao.stream.ble/link-down\n            :dao.stream.ble/link-down]\n           (events-of {:deposits deposits})))\n    (is (= [[:stop-radio]] actions))))\n\n\n(deftest frames-deposit-as-events-with-exact-bytes\n  (let [!now (atom 0)\n        s (state !now)\n        {:keys [deposits]} (links/handle-radio-event s [:frame peer (octets->bytes [1 2 3])])]\n    (is (= 1 (count deposits)))\n    (is (ble/frame-event? (first deposits)))\n    (is (= peer (:dao.stream.ble/source (first deposits))))\n    (is (= [1 2 3] (octets-of\n                    (base64/decode (:dao.stream.ble/bytes (first deposits))))))))\n\n\n(deftest inbound-frames-over-the-budget-are-never-deposited\n  (let [!now (atom 0)\n        s (state !now :max-frame-bytes 4)\n        over (octets->bytes [1 2 3 4 5])\n        at (octets->bytes [1 2 3 4])]\n    (is (= [] (events-of (links/handle-radio-event s [:frame peer over]))))\n    (is (= 1 (count (:deposits (links/handle-radio-event s [:frame peer at])))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The send rule\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(deftest a-send-without-a-link-is-the-clean-transport-error\n  (let [!now (atom 0)\n        s (state !now)\n        {:keys [state outcome deposits actions]}\n        (links/send! s peer (octets->bytes [1]))]\n    (is (= :dao.stream/transport-error (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)))\n    (is (= \"no link to peer\" (:dao.stream.ble/reason outcome)))\n    (is (= [:dao.stream.ble/send-failed] (events-of {:deposits deposits})))\n    (is (= peer (:dao.stream.ble/peer (first deposits))))\n    (is (= [] actions))\n    (is (= s state))))\n\n\n(deftest a-send-over-a-link-is-an-action-and-ok\n  (let [!now (atom 0)\n        s (:state (links/handle-radio-event (state !now) [:link-up peer :central]))\n        {:keys [outcome deposits actions]} (links/send! s peer (octets->bytes [1 2]))]\n    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)))\n    (is (= [] deposits))\n    (is (= [[:send-frame peer [1 2]]]\n           (mapv (fn [[k p bs]] [k p (octets-of bs)]) actions)))))\n\n\n(deftest a-malformed-destination-fails-without-a-link-check\n  (let [!now (atom 0)\n        s (state !now)\n        {:keys [outcome deposits actions]} (links/send! s \"\" (octets->bytes [1]))]\n    (is (= :dao.stream/transport-error (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)))\n    (is (= \"malformed destination\" (:dao.stream.ble/reason outcome)))\n    (is (= 1 (count deposits)))\n    (is (= [] actions))))\n\n\n(deftest a-send-fail-the-host-reports-later-is-a-deposit\n  (let [!now (atom 0)\n20:(defn- ring\n27:(defn- octets->bytes\n34:(defn- writer\n55:(defn- make-mesh\n69:(defn- delivered\n78:(defn- link-all!\n91:(deftest two-nodes-exchange-one-value-once\n117:(deftest a-send-before-any-link-is-ok-and-unspent\n128:(deftest both-directions-redundancy-is-eaten-by-the-dedup\n149:(deftest a-middle-node-relays-and-the-loop-dies-at-the-dedup\n178:(deftest ttl-zero-delivers-locally-and-relays-nothing\n196:(deftest ttl-one-reaches-exactly-two-hops\n222:(deftest the-seq-is-spent-when-the-raw-writer-accepted-the-frame\n241:(deftest different-origins-never-share-a-dedup-key\n259:(deftest the-dedup-cache-is-bounded-oldest-evicted\n289:(deftest foreign-frames-are-skipped-silently\n321:(deftest an-oversize-value-is-refused-by-the-raw-writer\n337:(deftest a-raw-gap-is-adopted-and-loses-what-the-ring-lost\n365:(deftest one-dead-neighbor-starves-nothing\n388:(deftest a-gap-leaves-the-neighbor-set-stale-and-usable\n427:(deftest a-closed-raw-layer-clears-the-neighbor-set\n439:(deftest a-wire-ttl-above-the-budget-is-clamped\n   dropped — this is the loop breaker and the redundancy eater, and it is\n   bounded: `:max-remembered` `[origin seq]` keys, oldest evicted first.\n   There is no clock and no freshness judgment in the cache: a replayed\n   old sequence outside the cache window is re-delivered and re-relayed,\n   and idempotence of the payload is the payload's, the same rule the\n   Writing section of `dao.stream.md` states for retries.\n2. **Local delivery.** One event deposited on the mesh's own deposit\n   medium (the composition wires an evicting ring, for the datagram\n   reasons): `{:dao.stream.ble.mesh/source peer :dao.stream.ble.mesh/origin\n   o :dao.stream.ble.mesh/seq n :dao.stream.ble.mesh/value v}`. Readers\n   hold their own cursors on it; a `gap` there is mesh values lost, to be\n   handled by the reader's loss policy.\n3. **Relay.** When the received `ttl` is positive, re-emit the frame with\n   `ttl` decremented — clamped to this mesh's own configured `:ttl`, so\n   a frame claiming a large budget amplifies only as far as the\n   configuration this composition chose — toward **every current\n   neighbor except the source peer**. The neighbor set is the raw\n   layer's: the mesh reads it from the traffic stream's\n   `link-up`/`link-down` lifecycle events as it steps, holding its own\n   neighbor table as data. A `closed` from the raw layer clears it —\n   the node itself is gone. A `gap` on the raw ring may leave the set\n   stale, and stale is the honest choice: a dead neighbor's relays\n   answer `send-failed` and cost nothing, a cleared set would cost the\n   mesh every relay it has, and a stable link emits no `link-up` to\n   refill what a clear emptied. The next `link-down` corrects the\n   staleness. There is no route computation — flooding is the whole of\n   routing, which section 2's peer-address rule makes honest rather\n   than lazy. Relay sends answer non-`ok` to nothing: a failed relay is\n   a lost frame, flooding tolerates loss, and the raw traffic stream's\n   `send-failed` events are the data a composition that wants to\n   observe loss observes. A frame received with `ttl` 0 delivers\n   locally and relays nothing.\n\nForeign frames — not this layer's values — are skipped, never answered,\nnever diagnosed on any shared stream (`dao.stream.datagram.md` 6).\n\n## 8. The dart seam (`dao.stream.ble/dart`)\n\nThe first host seam targets the Flutter app (Android, iOS, macOS). Two\nplugins, both pinned exact and both BSD-3:\n\n- **Central role:** `flutter_blue_plus` **1.36.8** — scan, connect,\n  discover the mesh service, subscribe to its TX characteristic's\n  notifications, write its RX one. The 2.x line changed to a license\n  that is not free for for-profit use, and this repository is\n  GPL-2.0-only with a linking exception, so the pin is exact and a\n  2.x upgrade is an owner decision, not a dependency bump.\n- **Peripheral role:** `flutter_ble_peripheral` **3.1.0** — advertise\n  the service UUID, serve GATT: receive writes, notify subscribers.\n  Android, iOS, macOS and Windows only — no Linux implementation — so a\n  Linux host runs the central role alone: it scans, dials, and\n  exchanges frames with every advertising peer, but never advertises or\n  serves. The seam handles the missing role honestly rather than dying:\n  a refused start deposits `bind-failed` as data and the node runs.\n\nThe adapter holds no policy: it maps plugin callbacks into radio events,\nhands them to `dao.stream.ble.links`, appends the returned deposits in\norder, performs the returned actions, and exposes `{:send! f :close! f}`\nwhose `send!` is the send rule of section 6. Platform facts it must\nclassify, not hide: the peripheral role's GattWrite carries no central\nidentity, so that whole role is one logical link at one synthetic peer\naddress (`peripheral-peer`) — the mesh's dedup eats the copies, and\n   the relay rule's exclusion of the source has a hub consequence a\n   composition must know: a frame that arrived through the peripheral\n   role is never relayed back out through it, so a node whose neighbors\n   are all centrals of its own GATT server does not route between them;\niOS cannot advertise manufacturer data, so the advertisement carries the\nservice UUID alone and every in-band identity travels in frames;\nbackground restrictions suspend advertising and scanning, so a\nsuspended node loses its links and binds again only when the\ncomposition re-binds. Every plugin future is caught: a platform refusal\nthe composition should see as data (`bind-failed`, `send-fail`,\n`radio-down`, `link-failed`) is deposited or fed to the machine, never\nthrown across the seam. Permissions are the app's: Android needs\n`BLUETOOTH_SCAN` (with `neverForLocation` — the mesh profile scans for\nits own service UUID, never for beacon-derived location),\n`BLUETOOTH_CONNECT`, `BLUETOOTH_ADVERTISE`; iOS needs\n`NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription`; a sandboxed macOS app needs\n`com.apple.security.device.bluetooth` in both entitlements files plus\nthe same usage string in `macos/Runner/Info.plist`.\n\nThe seam is explicitly local and non-migratable (`datom.world.md`, Host\nBoundaries): it is the one piece of this stack that cannot run on a host\nwith no radio, and a composition on such a host composes the same\nportable layers over a different seam.\n\n**The device-test plan.** The sandbox cannot reach a plugin call, so\nthese facts are proven on real radios, in this order: (1) two devices\nbind — each traffic stream shows `bound`, then `peer-seen` per peer,\nthen `link-up` in both roles; (2) a mesh send from one device delivers\nonce on the other, over however many links carried it; (3) a third\ndevice out of range of the first receives through the middle one — the\nrelay; (4) bluetooth switched off mid-run deposits `closed` and\n`link-down` for every peer, and sends answer `transport-error`; (5)\nairplane-mode recovery re-binds and re-learns; (6) an Android peripheral\nand an iOS central exchange frames — the profile's cross-platform half.\n\n## 9. Exposure\n\nA raw writer handle entered in a mirror table\n(`dao.stream.remote.md` 2) lets whoever reaches it send arbitrary frames\nfrom this radio. No composition does so without a gate on that entry.\n\n## 10. What S2 holds\n\n- **Fragmentation**: the udp fragment envelope over mesh frames, so one\n  value may exceed one raw frame's budget, with the two reassembly bounds\n  and their eviction rules.\n- **`dao.stream.remote` over the mesh**: mirror, reflection and link\n  composed over the mesh value medium, which is what makes a `yin.repl`\n  session survive the loss of every IP route.\n- **Gateway nodes**: a composition with both a radio seam and an IP seam\n  forwarding between the mesh medium and a `dao.stream.datagram` medium —\n  an ordinary forwarder interpreter, no new machinery.\n- **Gossip reduction**: S1 floods every frame to every neighbor; a\n  probability- or frontier-based relay policy is an interpreter change,\n  not a wire change, because the wire carries only origin, seq, ttl,\n  value.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"The portable code contains the listed gap, TTL, sequence, fan-out, and link-accounting fixes. The new inbound-ceiling test states the documented law correctly. I found a likely missing fix in Dart startup: `start-radio!` calls the async peripheral starter without `await`, then emits `radio-up`. I’m checking the generated Dart to confirm the effect."}}
