{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.ble.md | sed -n '210,225p;370,430p'; sed -n '77,150p' /Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_ble_peripheral-3.1.0/lib/src/flutter_ble_peripheral.dart; rg -n 'cancel|onValueReceived|connectionState' /Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_blue_plus-1.36.8/lib/src/bluetooth_device.dart /Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_blue_plus-1.36.8/lib/src/bluetooth_characteristic.dart\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.ble.md | sed -n '210,225p;370,430p'; sed -n '77,150p' /Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_ble_peripheral-3.1.0/lib/src/flutter_ble_peripheral.dart; rg -n 'cancel|onValueReceived|connectionState' /Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_blue_plus-1.36.8/lib/src/bluetooth_device.dart /Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_blue_plus-1.36.8/lib/src/bluetooth_characteristic.dart\"","aggregated_output":"   210\t  alone, because silence is not a fact a radio reports.\n   211\t- Capacity is counted in events. One event is at most `:max-frame-bytes`\n   212\t  of payload as Base64, so memory is bounded by\n   213\t  `capacity * ceil(max-frame-bytes * 4 / 3)` plus envelope.\n   214\t\n   215\t## 6. The link state machine (`dao.stream.ble.links`)\n   216\t\n   217\tA seam's judgment is all link bookkeeping, and link bookkeeping is the\n   218\tsame on every host, so it lives host-free: `dao.stream.ble.links` is a\n   219\tpure state machine over **radio events**, and `seam` is the generic\n   220\thost-free adapter that composes the machine into the seam contract of\n   221\tsection 3. A host seam (section 8) is then only a translator: plugin\n   222\tstreams in, radio events out; actions out, plugin calls in. The dart\n   223\tseam holds no policy of its own; a seam cannot drift from the tests\n   224\tthat gate the machine.\n   225\t\n   370\t   the node itself is gone. A `gap` on the raw ring may leave the set\n   371\t   stale, and stale is the honest choice: a dead neighbor's relays\n   372\t   answer `send-failed` and cost nothing, a cleared set would cost the\n   373\t   mesh every relay it has, and a stable link emits no `link-up` to\n   374\t   refill what a clear emptied. The next `link-down` corrects the\n   375\t   staleness. There is no route computation — flooding is the whole of\n   376\t   routing, which section 2's peer-address rule makes honest rather\n   377\t   than lazy. Relay sends answer non-`ok` to nothing: a failed relay is\n   378\t   a lost frame, flooding tolerates loss, and the raw traffic stream's\n   379\t   `send-failed` events are the data a composition that wants to\n   380\t   observe loss observes. A frame received with `ttl` 0 delivers\n   381\t   locally and relays nothing.\n   382\t\n   383\tForeign frames — not this layer's values — are skipped, never answered,\n   384\tnever diagnosed on any shared stream (`dao.stream.datagram.md` 6).\n   385\t\n   386\t## 8. The dart seam (`dao.stream.ble/dart`)\n   387\t\n   388\tThe first host seam targets the Flutter app (Android, iOS, macOS). Two\n   389\tplugins, both pinned exact and both BSD-3:\n   390\t\n   391\t- **Central role:** `flutter_blue_plus` **1.36.8** — scan, connect,\n   392\t  discover the mesh service, subscribe to its TX characteristic's\n   393\t  notifications, write its RX one. The 2.x line changed to a license\n   394\t  that is not free for for-profit use, and this repository is\n   395\t  GPL-2.0-only with a linking exception, so the pin is exact and a\n   396\t  2.x upgrade is an owner decision, not a dependency bump.\n   397\t- **Peripheral role:** `flutter_ble_peripheral` **3.1.0** — advertise\n   398\t  the service UUID, serve GATT: receive writes, notify subscribers.\n   399\t  Android, iOS, macOS and Windows only — no Linux implementation — so a\n   400\t  Linux host runs the central role alone: it scans, dials, and\n   401\t  exchanges frames with every advertising peer, but never advertises or\n   402\t  serves. The seam handles the missing role honestly rather than dying:\n   403\t  a refused start deposits `bind-failed` as data and the node runs.\n   404\t\n   405\tThe adapter holds no policy: it maps plugin callbacks into radio events,\n   406\thands them to `dao.stream.ble.links`, appends the returned deposits in\n   407\torder, performs the returned actions, and exposes `{:send! f :close! f}`\n   408\twhose `send!` is the send rule of section 6. Platform facts it must\n   409\tclassify, not hide: the peripheral role's GattWrite carries no central\n   410\tidentity, so that whole role is one logical link at one synthetic peer\n   411\taddress (`peripheral-peer`) — the mesh's dedup eats the copies, and\n   412\t   the relay rule's exclusion of the source has a hub consequence a\n   413\t   composition must know: a frame that arrived through the peripheral\n   414\t   role is never relayed back out through it, so a node whose neighbors\n   415\t   are all centrals of its own GATT server does not route between them;\n   416\tiOS cannot advertise manufacturer data, so the advertisement carries the\n   417\tservice UUID alone and every in-band identity travels in frames;\n   418\tbackground restrictions suspend advertising and scanning, so a\n   419\tsuspended node loses its links and binds again only when the\n   420\tcomposition re-binds. Every plugin future is caught: a platform refusal\n   421\tthe composition should see as data (`bind-failed`, `send-fail`,\n   422\t`radio-down`, `link-failed`) is deposited or fed to the machine, never\n   423\tthrown across the seam. Permissions are the app's: Android needs\n   424\t`BLUETOOTH_SCAN` (with `neverForLocation` — the mesh profile scans for\n   425\tits own service UUID, never for beacon-derived location),\n   426\t`BLUETOOTH_CONNECT`, `BLUETOOTH_ADVERTISE`; iOS needs\n   427\t`NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription`; a sandboxed macOS app needs\n   428\t`com.apple.security.device.bluetooth` in both entitlements files plus\n   429\tthe same usage string in `macos/Runner/Info.plist`.\n   430\t\n  /// Platform-specific settings:\n  /// - Android: [androidSettings]\n  /// - iOS/macOS: [darwinSettings]\n  /// - Windows: [windowsSettings]\n  ///\n  /// Returns [PeripheralBluetoothState.ready] once the advertisement is on air.\n  /// On Apple platforms a state such as [PeripheralBluetoothState.turnedOff] is\n  /// returned when the radio is not up yet; the advertisement is queued and\n  /// starts as soon as it is. A platform that refuses the advertisement\n  /// outright throws a [PlatformException] instead.\n  Future<PeripheralBluetoothState> start({\n    required AdvertiseDataCore advertiseData,\n\n    /// Serve a GATT service alongside the advertisement. Leave this null to\n    /// advertise only.\n    GattServerSettings? gattServer,\n\n    // Platform-specific settings\n    AndroidAdvertiseSettings? androidSettings,\n    DarwinAdvertiseSettings? darwinSettings,\n    WindowsAdvertiseSettings? windowsSettings,\n  }) async {\n    final parameters = advertiseData.toJson();\n\n    // The bytes are sent raw as well, so the native side can read a byte\n    // buffer rather than decoding the converter's int list.\n    if (advertiseData.manufacturerData != null) {\n      parameters['manufacturerDataBytes'] = advertiseData.manufacturerData;\n    }\n\n    if (advertiseData.serviceUuids != null) {\n      parameters['serviceUuids'] = advertiseData.serviceUuids;\n    }\n\n    if (gattServer != null) {\n      final serviceUuid = gattServer.serviceUuid ?? advertiseData.serviceUuid;\n      if (serviceUuid == null) {\n        throw ArgumentError(\n          'A GATT service needs a uuid. Set either '\n          'AdvertiseDataCore.serviceUuid or GattServerSettings.serviceUuid.',\n        );\n      }\n      final characteristics = gattServer.effectiveCharacteristics;\n      if (characteristics.any((c) => c.properties.isEmpty)) {\n        throw ArgumentError(\n          'A GATT characteristic needs at least one property.',\n        );\n      }\n      final uuids = characteristics.map((c) => c.uuid.toLowerCase()).toSet();\n      if (uuids.length != characteristics.length) {\n        throw ArgumentError(\n          'A GATT service cannot serve the same characteristic uuid twice.',\n        );\n      }\n      parameters['gattServiceUuid'] = serviceUuid;\n      parameters['gattCharacteristics'] =\n          characteristics.map((c) => c.toJson()).toList();\n    }\n\n    // Android settings\n    if (Platform.isAndroid && androidSettings != null) {\n      // Automatically set the advertiseSet flag based on which parameters\n      // are provided.\n      final useExtendedAdvertising =\n          androidSettings.advertiseSetParameters != null;\n      parameters['advertiseSet'] = useExtendedAdvertising;\n\n      // Legacy advertising settings\n      if (androidSettings.advertiseSettings != null) {\n        final json = androidSettings.advertiseSettings!.toJson();\n        for (final key in json.keys) {\n          parameters[key] = json[key];\n        }\n      }\n/Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_blue_plus-1.36.8/lib/src/bluetooth_characteristic.dart:85:  Stream<List<int>> get onValueReceived => FlutterBluePlusPlatform.instance.onCharacteristicReceived\n/Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_blue_plus-1.36.8/lib/src/bluetooth_characteristic.dart:353:  @Deprecated('Use onValueReceived instead')\n/Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_blue_plus-1.36.8/lib/src/bluetooth_characteristic.dart:354:  Stream<List<int>> get onValueChangedStream => onValueReceived;\n/Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_blue_plus-1.36.8/lib/src/bluetooth_device.dart:53:  /// Register a subscription to be canceled when the device is disconnected.\n/Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_blue_plus-1.36.8/lib/src/bluetooth_device.dart:57:  ///   - [next] if true, the the stream will be canceled only on the *next* disconnection.\n/Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_blue_plus-1.36.8/lib/src/bluetooth_device.dart:59:  ///   - [delayed] Note: This option is only meant for `connectionState` subscriptions.\n/Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_blue_plus-1.36.8/lib/src/bluetooth_device.dart:60:  ///     When `true`, we cancel after a small delay. This ensures the `connectionState`\n/Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_blue_plus-1