{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ble/mesh.cljc | sed -n '288,310p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ble/links.cljc | sed -n '305,330p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.ble.md | sed -n '146,161p;192,204p'; sed -n '1,95p' /Users/sto/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_ble_peripheral-3.1.0/lib/src/flutter_ble_peripheral.dart; rg -n 'Future|cancel' lib/cljd-out/dao/stream/ble/dart.dart | tail -10\"","aggregated_output":"   288\t  \"One raw traffic event consumed into the mesh: lifecycle events keep\n   289\t   the neighbor set current, frame events deliver and relay. Answers\n   290\t   {:delivered n :relayed n}, zeros for a skipped event.\"\n   291\t  [mesh v]\n   292\t  (cond\n   293\t    (ble/lifecycle-event? v)\n   294\t    (do (case (:dao.stream.ble/event v)\n   295\t          :dao.stream.ble/link-up\n   296\t          (swap! mesh update :neighbors conj (:dao.stream.ble/peer v))\n   297\t          :dao.stream.ble/link-down\n   298\t          (swap! mesh update :neighbors disj (:dao.stream.ble/peer v))\n   299\t          :dao.stream.ble/peer-lost\n   300\t          (swap! mesh update :neighbors disj (:dao.stream.ble/peer v))\n   301\t          ;; The raw layer says the node itself is gone: every link fact\n   302\t          ;; this mesh held is stale, the same rule a gap gets below.\n   303\t          :dao.stream.ble/closed\n   304\t          (swap! mesh assoc :neighbors #{})\n   305\t          nil)\n   306\t        {:delivered 0 :relayed 0})\n   307\t\n   308\t    (ble/frame-event? v)\n   309\t    (let [source (:dao.stream.ble/source v)\n   310\t          f (decode-frame (:dao.stream.ble/bytes v))]\n   305\t  (doseq [ev deposits]\n   306\t    (try (stream/append! deposit ev)\n   307\t         (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n   308\t\n   309\t\n   310\t(defn seam\n   311\t  \"The generic adapter (design 6): the machine composed into the seam\n   312\t   contract `dao.stream.ble/writer` consumes, over a `radio` map the\n   313\t   host supplies:\n   314\t\n   315\t     {:perform! (fn [action])}   machine -> radio: [:connect peer],\n   316\t                                 [:send-frame peer bytes], [:stop-radio]\n   317\t\n   318\t   and answers {:send! f :close! f :radio! f :state f}: `:send!`/\n   319\t   `:close!` are the seam contract (bind data in, those two out, deposits\n   320\t   flowing to `:deposit` only); `:radio!` is the adapter's one entry, one\n   321\t   radio event in; `:state` observes the machine, for tests. `:send!`\n   322\t   hands the frame to the radio and answers `ok` -- it asserts nothing\n   323\t   about the air -- and a failure the host reports later arrives as a\n   324\t   [:send-fail ...] radio event, the send-failed channel of design 4.\n   325\t   The radio's own send failures are deposited; they are not retried.\"\n   326\t  [{:keys [identity deposit max-frame-bytes max-links announce-window-ms\n   327\t           now-ms radio]}]\n   328\t  (when-not (and (map? radio) (fn? (:perform! radio)))\n   329\t    (throw (ex-info \"a dao.stream.ble seam needs a radio with :perform!\"\n   330\t                    {:radio radio})))\n   146\t  beyond it.\n   147\t- `:announce-window-ms` — the discovery throttle (section 5), default\n   148\t  2000.\n   149\t- `:now-ms` — the clock the throttle reads, `(f)` → integer\n   150\t  milliseconds. A host seam supplies the host clock; the state machine\n   151\t  (section 6) takes it as data, so tests and the simulation supply a\n   152\t  deterministic clock. **The clock is the seam's own operational fact**,\n   153\t  like the socket a datagram seam binds: no protocol state below the seam\n   154\t  reads it, and `dao.stream.udp`'s no-clock rule for protocol state\n   155\t  stands.\n   156\t\n   157\t## 4. The writer handle\n   158\t\n   159\tDeclared surface: `#{:writer :closable}`. `descriptor` answers `ok` with\n   160\tthe descriptor above and its identity, before and after close.\n   161\t\n   192\t## 5. The traffic stream\n   193\t\n   194\t- The deposit destination is supplied by the composition and **must be an\n   195\t  evicting ring** (`dao.stream.ringbuffer`), for the datagram reasons: any\n   196\t  broadcaster on the air could grow a complete-history log without bound.\n   197\t- A ring never refuses, so the deposit-admission rule of `dao.stream.md`\n   198\t  (Surfaces) holds by construction. A `:dao.stream/gap` on the traffic\n   199\t  stream means frames and link facts were lost to this reader, and link\n   200\t  facts lost are link facts the reader must not pretend to hold.\n   201\t- **The discovery throttle.** Advertisements repeat many times a second.\n   202\t  Each observed advertisement of the service UUID deposits at most one\n   203\t  `:dao.stream.ble/peer-seen` event per peer per `:announce-window-ms` —\n   204\t  the latest RSSI wins. This is a host-side throttle over the medium's own\n/*\n * Copyright (c) 2022. Julian Steenbakker.\n * All rights reserved. Use of this source code is governed by a\n * BSD-style license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n */\n\nimport 'dart:async';\nimport 'dart:io';\n// Uint8List is part of the public API here, so it is imported explicitly\n// rather than relying on it leaking in through flutter/services.dart.\n// ignore: unnecessary_import\nimport 'dart:typed_data';\n\nimport 'package:flutter/services.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter_ble_peripheral/src/core/enums/peripheral_bluetooth_state.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter_ble_peripheral/src/core/enums/peripheral_state.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter_ble_peripheral/src/core/models/advertise_data_core.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter_ble_peripheral/src/core/models/gatt_server_settings.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter_ble_peripheral/src/core/models/gatt_write.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter_ble_peripheral/src/platform/android/models/android_advertise_data.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter_ble_peripheral/src/platform/android/models/android_advertise_settings.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter_ble_peripheral/src/platform/darwin/models/darwin_advertise_settings.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter_ble_peripheral/src/platform/windows/models/windows_advertise_settings.dart';\n\n/// Advertises this device as a BLE peripheral, and serves the GATT service\n/// that connected centrals read from and write to.\nclass FlutterBlePeripheral {\n  /// Returns the singleton instance.\n  factory FlutterBlePeripheral() {\n    return _instance;\n  }\n\n  FlutterBlePeripheral._internal();\n\n  /// Singleton instance\n  static final FlutterBlePeripheral _instance =\n      FlutterBlePeripheral._internal();\n\n  /// Method Channel used to communicate state with\n  static const MethodChannel _methodChannel = MethodChannel(\n    'dev.steenbakker.flutter_ble_peripheral/ble_state',\n  );\n\n  /// Event Channel for MTU state\n  final EventChannel _mtuChangedEventChannel = const EventChannel(\n    'dev.steenbakker.flutter_ble_peripheral/ble_mtu_changed',\n  );\n\n  /// Event Channel used to changed state\n  final EventChannel _stateChangedEventChannel = const EventChannel(\n    'dev.steenbakker.flutter_ble_peripheral/ble_state_changed',\n  );\n\n  /// Event Channel used to receive data\n  final EventChannel _dataReceivedEventChannel = const EventChannel(\n    'dev.steenbakker.flutter_ble_peripheral/ble_data_received',\n  );\n\n  /// Event Channel for TX subscription changes\n  final EventChannel _subscriptionChangedEventChannel = const EventChannel(\n    'dev.steenbakker.flutter_ble_peripheral/ble_subscription_changed',\n  );\n\n  Stream<int>? _mtuState;\n  Stream<PeripheralState>? _peripheralState;\n  Stream<GattWrite>? _gattWrites;\n  Stream<Uint8List>? _dataReceived;\n  Stream<GattSubscription>? _characteristicSubscriptions;\n  Stream<bool>? _subscriptionChanged;\n\n  /// Start advertising.\n  ///\n  /// [advertiseData] - Core advertising data. Use [AdvertiseDataCore] for\n  /// cross-platform, or platform-specific classes like [AndroidAdvertiseData]\n  /// for platform features.\n  ///\n  /// Platform-specific settings:\n  /// - Android: [androidSettings]\n  /// - iOS/macOS: [darwinSettings]\n  /// - Windows: [windowsSettings]\n  ///\n  /// Returns [PeripheralBluetoothState.ready] once the advertisement is on air.\n  /// On Apple platforms a state such as [PeripheralBluetoothState.turnedOff] is\n  /// returned when the radio is not up yet; the advertisement is queued and\n  /// starts as soon as it is. A platform that refuses the advertisement\n  /// outright throws a [PlatformException] instead.\n  Future<PeripheralBluetoothState> start({\n    required AdvertiseDataCore advertiseData,\n\n    /// Serve a GATT service alongside the advertisement. Leave this null to\n    /// advertise only.\n    GattServerSettings? gattServer,\n\n    // Platform-specific settings\n    AndroidAdvertiseSettings? androidSettings,\n269:da.Future<void> release$BANG_$1(dc.dynamic d$1, ){\n576:final da.Future<void> $1=((some$11203_$AUTO_$1 as f_flutter_ble_peripheral.FlutterBlePeripheral).sendData(arg$1, characteristicUuid: $if_$3, ));\n636:final da.Future<void> $2=((rx$1 as f_flutter_blue_plus.BluetoothCharacteristic).write(casted$1, withoutResponse: false, ));\n759:((s$1 as da.StreamSubscription).cancel());\n836:final da.Future<f_flutter_ble_peripheral.PeripheralBluetoothState> $1=(p$1.start(advertiseData: f_flutter_ble_peripheral.AdvertiseDataCore(serviceUuid: $if_$1, ), gattServer: f_flutter_ble_peripheral.GattServerSettings(serviceUuid: $if_$2, txCharacteristicUuid: (tx_uuid$1 as dc.String), rxCharacteristicUuid: (rx_uuid$1 as dc.String), ), ));\n935:final da.Future<void> $1=(f_flutter_blue_plus.FlutterBluePlus.startScan(withServices: casted$1, continuousUpdates: true, oneByOne: true, ));\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"Generated Dart confirms the startup defect: it stores a `Future` as the peripheral object and emits `radio-up` before that future completes. Peripheral sends and shutdown then cast that stored value to `FlutterBlePeripheral`.\n\nThe JVM suite passes independently at 51 tests / 203 assertions. The new ceiling test contributes only 3 assertions, so it accounts for 50/200 → 51/203, not the reported lost-tree count of 50/198. I also found silent send drops for TX-only peers and scan/adapter subscriptions missing from shutdown’s subscription list."}}
