{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljd/dao/stream/ble/dart.cljd | sed -n '85,125p;241,282p;340,353p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ble/links.cljc | sed -n '276,297p'; nl -ba test/dao/stream/ble/links_test.cljc | sed -n '134,148p'; sed -n '365,427p' test/dao/stream/ble/mesh_test.cljc; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"    85\t             ^fbp/BluetoothDevice d (.-device sr)]\n    86\t         (radio! [:adv (.-str (.-remoteId d)) (.-rssi sr)]))))\n    87\t   (fn [e] (radio! [:radio-down (str \"scan: \" e)]))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn- adapter-events!\n    91\t  \"The adapter going off -- unavailable, unauthorized, turning off, off\n    92\t   -- is the radio stopping on its own. The stream starts at :unknown\n    93\t   and passes through :turningOn on the way up; neither is a stop, and\n    94\t   treating them as one tears the node down at bind.\"\n    95\t  [radio!]\n    96\t  (listen!\n    97\t   fbp/FlutterBluePlus.adapterState\n    98\t   (fn [state]\n    99\t     (when (contains? #{fbp/BluetoothAdapterState.unavailable\n   100\t                        fbp/BluetoothAdapterState.unauthorized\n   101\t                        fbp/BluetoothAdapterState.turningOff\n   102\t                        fbp/BluetoothAdapterState.off}\n   103\t                      state)\n   104\t       (radio! [:radio-down (str \"adapter state: \" state)])))\n   105\t   (fn [e] (radio! [:radio-down (str \"adapter: \" e)]))))\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn- watch-central!\n   109\t  \"One connectionState watcher per dialed device, installed once -- the\n   110\t   subscription kept in !subs so a stop tears it down: the link going\n   111\t   down is a radio event, whatever the cause. Installed only after the\n   112\t   connection is live: the stream emits its current value on listen, so\n   113\t   a pre-connect watcher would announce a disconnected